        "original_id": "c7630ef9-b4dc-5dbc-bc57-dd50693cef1b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Jackson, Joe Strummer, John Graham Mellor\n- Organizations: the Clash\n- Works: Moonwalk\n- Topics: music, autobiography, punk rock\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Jackson was born on August 29, 1958, and he was an American singer, songwriter, and dancer.\n- John Graham Mellor was born on August 21, 1952, and he was known by the stage name Joe Strummer.\n- The Clash was a punk rock band formed in 1976 as part of the original wave of British punk.\n- Joe Strummer was an English musician, singer, actor, and songwriter who co-founded the Clash and served as its lyricist, rhythm guitarist, and lead vocalist.\n- Moonwalk is a 1988 autobiography written by American recording artist Michael Jackson.\n- Joe Strummer died on December 22, 2002.\n- Michael Jackson died on June 25, 2009.",
